      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T14:17:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it\u0027s interesting because this (not overloading on arrays) is the one way `sk_sp` isn\u0027t just a `std::unique_ptr` with a copy-constructor (which refs) and a deleter that unrefs.\n\nI\u0027ve seen a number of comments around which are basically, \"why couldn\u0027t the array version of `std::unique_ptr` have been given a different name (like `std::unique_array_ptr`)\" so that one could use deduction guides with it usefully.",
      "parentUuid": "55165f04_f3ad3074",
